==English==

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|la-ecc|abbreviātor}}. Compare {{cog|fr|abbréviateur}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/əˈbɹiː.viˌeɪ.tɚ/|/-ɛɪ.tɚ/}}
* {{a|GenAm}} {{IPA|en|/əˈbɹi.viˌeɪ.tɚ/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-PerfectSoundWhatever-abbreviator.wav|Audio (CA)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A person who [[abbreviates]] or [[shortens]]. {{defdate|from early 16th c.}}<ref name=SOED>{{R:SOED5|page=3}}</ref>
# {{lb|en|Roman Catholicism|historical}} One of a college of [[seventy-two]] officers of the [[papal]] court whose duty was to make a short minute of a decision on a [[petition]], or reply of the pope to a letter, and [[afterwards]] [[expand]] the minute into official form. {{defdate|from mid-16th c.}}<ref name=SOED/>

